  "entry": "code/README.md",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Shows what a pChEMBL-style exact-value filter removes from an IC50 table, and uses pooled and per-paper censored-normal (Tobit) models, a pooled-versus-within-paper comparison of two targets and a top-value tie test to estimate the resulting bias. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
